### Phase 6 — Resilience4j (Food → Booking)

Fallback is **503**, not a fake booking. Watch **food-service** logs for retries and `Booking circuit CLOSED -> OPEN`.

### Circuit state (no JWT required)
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/circuitbreakers

GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health

### Place order while Booking is up — 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/food/orders
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hotelId": 1,
  "bookingId": 1,
  "roomNumber": "101",
  "items": [
    { "menuItemId": 1, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Demo: stop booking-service, then place several orders
# Expect 503, retry logs, then circuit OPEN (Feign skipped)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/food/orders
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hotelId": 1,
  "bookingId": 1,
  "roomNumber": "101",
  "items": [
    { "menuItemId": 1, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Missing booking still 404 (must not open the circuit)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/999999
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
